It isn't clear to me if you are having problems with just shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>, or locally as well.
But for shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>, you generally do not want to use setwd (see the Troubleshooting section of the documentation <http://docs.rstudio.com/shinyapps.io/Troubleshooting.html>).
The section on accessing your local database <http://docs.rstudio.com/shinyapps.io/applications.html#accessing-your-local-databases-from-shinyapps.io> is being updated this week, and I will be posting an announcement to the group, to recommend the use of the "odbc" package which makes the RStudio Professional Drivers <https://www.rstudio.com/products/drivers/> available on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>
If you must use "ROracle", you will likely need to open an issue or pull request in shinyapps-package-dependencies <https://github.com/rstudio/shinyapps-package-dependencies> so that the Oracle client can be installed.

