I am trying to create a Shiny app that will take a word as the input and predict the next word, based on information I have from blogs, news, and twitter. I am using R programming and have created ngram.rds that involved making a corpus, then tokenizing it, and finally creating an ngram.

This is what I have on my server.R for my Shiny app:

    library(shiny)

    library(rsconnect)

    library(tm)

    library(data.table)

    library(quanteda)

    library(dplyr)

        server <- shinyServer(function(input, output) {

       homed <- (getwd())

      setwd(homed)

        wp<- reactive({

              ngram <- readRDS("ngram.rds")

              y <- kwic(ngram, input)

             ydt <- as.data.table(y)

            ychar <- as.character(ydt)

            ydfm <- dfm(ychar, remove_punct=TRUE, remove_numbers=TRUE)

            w <- textstat_frequency(ydfm)

            wordPrediction <- w[[2,1]]

      wordPrediction

       })

      output$wordPrediction <- renderPrint({

               wp()

        })

       })

I am attaching what the logs on the dashboard told me. I have already upgraded to a more powerful subscription and that does not help, so I am not sure what the issue is. Also I am including the other errors I have found and the sizes of my files.  The application also runs very slowly on the shiny server but it works fine on just the R console, so I am not sure if that is related.

I am very much a beginner so I am not sure if there is something obvious that I am missing.

If someone can help me with this very soon I would really appreciate it! This is for an assignment that is due today and it is crucial that I get it done on time.

